# psql connection

`ConnectionStrings:Postgres` in appsettings is **Npgsql** format. Do **not** pass it to `psql`.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — psql: invalid connection option "Host"
psql "Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=aib;Username=jeremy"

# ✅ GOOD — flags
psql -h localhost -p 5432 -U jeremy -d aib

# ✅ GOOD — URI
psql "postgresql://jeremy@localhost:5432/aib"
```

Read host/port/db/user from `backend/Aib.Api/appsettings.Development.json` (or `appsettings.json`) and map to `-h` / `-p` / `-d` / `-U`.
